{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> each has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> share one point of tangency. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has a point of tangency with the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2a482b08ddebc962ed9858ddab94a3db7140e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> What is the area inside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> but outside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d3713b61d71855f44ce52196d5bf838501d09ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B?$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84b9e326bd427c8608100174e752c08642c3129.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1.1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(2,0), C=(1,-1); pair M=(1,0); pair D=(2,-1); dot (A); dot (B); dot (C); dot (D); dot (M);  draw(Circle(A,1)); draw(Circle(B,1)); draw(Circle(C,1));  draw(A--B); draw(M--D); draw(D--B);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"212\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a9e36ae8bcbfbe44df46ac571d86ac36a7fafac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 - \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1+\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"443\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84b9e326bd427c8608100174e752c08642c3129.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1.1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(2,0), C=(1,-1); pair M=(1,0); pair D=(2,-1); dot (A); dot (B); dot (C); dot (D); dot (M);  draw(Circle(A,1)); draw(Circle(B,1)); draw(Circle(C,1));  draw(A--B); draw(M--D); draw(D--B);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"212\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p>The requested area is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> minus the area shared between circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the other intersection of circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The area shared between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the regions between arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d7466b39123bcd705f40246fe2d2b59eb2749a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat {MD}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"19\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b31782c8439bb79194a830084c6c61a1feb22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MD}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" />, which is (considering the arc on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) a quarter of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/8418b1ef0e57b381ef7a6380aeda2b78bb76ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MDB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/952af8bd9a6b3237f46739b850d7ebd16790e3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi r^2}{4}-\\frac{bh}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e8057a4afc7344fb96c6dfb7f74dfb3478c44981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = h = r = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>(We can assume this because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/8642b7c5cd1300d35caeaeb0547bb040af5f8eff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBM$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> is 90 degrees, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7441715d996526e8f5fcdee56db17df4636e04bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDBM$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> is a square, due to the application of the tangent chord theorem at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p>So the area of the small region is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b879b6e7a19d0ce8fc8ffd8fa6030c34280e552c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The requested area is area of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> minus 4 of this area:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3aabaa32646cbee6258f410482422c444b897e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi 1^2 - 4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\pi - \\pi + 2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"273\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9b68aaa5462a2128fb5d06e10449ebc58b641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84b9e326bd427c8608100174e752c08642c3129.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1.1cm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), B=(2,0), C=(1,-1); pair M=(1,0); pair D=(2,-1); dot (A); dot (B); dot (C); dot (D); dot (M);  draw(Circle(A,1)); draw(Circle(B,1)); draw(Circle(C,1));  draw(A--B); draw(M--D); draw(D--B);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,W); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"212\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p>We can move the area above the part of the circle above the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> down, and similarly for the other side. Then, we have a square, whose diagonal is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the area is then just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/bafb067da4a3a0312073f193bb209921c2ebf029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{2 = C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"150\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~ Minor Edits, Challengees24\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can approach the problem by analyzing the overlapping regions of the figures. Let the regions associated with the triangles be denoted as follows: let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> represent the two small congruent triangles, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> represent the primary region from which we subtract the overlapping components to find our desired area.\n</p><p>We can find the two small congruent overlapping segments from triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and subtract them from the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to find our answer. We can see that half of each overlapping segment is a quarter circle minus an isosceles right triangle of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. This means that the area of half of the intersecting region is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a63e527bcc78167cee2e418de3f53698a937e2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now we need to multiply this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the area of the whole intersecting region:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a98d6de5d1479500c0215cfacd643621c3b4dbbe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac{1}{2} \\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We now multiply this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to find the total area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> intersecting regions, which gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a48820d1ab20dc95ae513d48798f0035b7a21be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1 \\right) = \\pi - 2\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting this total intersecting area from the area of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />), we find the area of the region of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that we are looking for:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7c083a8926a59b5602e99f3d3aab3970f3d2a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi - (\\pi - 2) = 2\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the final area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e8656291085c388b48a0fa8da85aed21c483bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />, which corresponds to option (D).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u23iWcqbJlE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u23iWcqbJlE</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=olRZuK11mAI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=olRZuK11mAI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath\">Video Solution by CanadaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/72h3E_CtW50?si=tyx26ImPeLpI7YK1&amp;t=8\">https://youtu.be/72h3E_CtW50?si=tyx26ImPeLpI7YK1&a